WEBVTT

00:00:15.090 --> 00:00:18.090
This will finish you, Yusei Fudo!

00:00:18.090 --> 00:00:20.930
Rhinotaurus attacks you directly!

00:00:22.450 --> 00:00:23.000
This is bad!

00:00:22.990 --> 00:00:23.960
Yusei!

00:00:25.420 --> 00:00:27.840
I have to use this to survive!

00:00:28.140 --> 00:00:30.700
I flip over my trap card Harmony Crystal!

00:00:31.030 --> 00:00:35.170
By removing a Synchro Monster and another 
monster in my graveyard from play...

00:00:35.170 --> 00:00:37.460
I can resurrect a Synchro 
Monster from my graveyard!

00:00:38.650 --> 00:00:44.980
I remove Junk Destroyer and Max Warrior in my 
graveyard from play to Special Summon Stardust Dragon!

00:00:47.730 --> 00:00:50.100
Rhinotaurus, stop your attack.

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:51.230
I'm not done!

00:00:51.230 --> 00:00:56.280
Due to Harmony Crystal's effect, you take damage 
equal to half of Stardust Dragon's attack points!

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:05.180
It succeeded!

00:01:05.320 --> 00:01:09.590
There's only a 50-point difference 
in Yusei Fudo and Jean's life points!

00:01:09.610 --> 00:01:14.350
He singlehandedly overcame a 
10,000-life-point difference to approach Jean!

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:17.530
Will we see a miracle?

00:01:34.940 --> 00:01:40.040
Every time you're hurt, you can become kinder

00:01:40.410 --> 00:01:45.580
Stand up and you'll understand strength

00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:50.050
Don't look back and keep going

00:01:50.290 --> 00:01:55.890
Both the past and the future 
are connected to the present

00:01:56.060 --> 00:02:00.870
There's no need to fear

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:08.540
I'll keep telling you that you're not alone

00:02:09.570 --> 00:02:14.510
The passionate emotions in your heart

00:02:15.250 --> 00:02:20.280
Streak to the infinite future

00:02:20.490 --> 00:02:25.690
Dreams surpass their limits

00:02:25.960 --> 00:02:33.800
And will lead you to a bright place

00:02:59.930 --> 00:03:05.860
Solely for Victory

00:03:09.480 --> 00:03:10.470
All right!

00:03:10.470 --> 00:03:12.370
Wow!  Just a little more!

00:03:12.370 --> 00:03:14.730
Yusei is going to turn it around!

00:03:15.380 --> 00:03:16.230
Yusei.

00:03:16.230 --> 00:03:21.560
Is this for real?  He 
caught up to Jean easily!

00:03:21.560 --> 00:03:24.710
Don't worry.  Look at his face.

00:03:28.980 --> 00:03:30.630
Too bad.

00:03:32.690 --> 00:03:38.030
You set Harmony Crystal on your first 
turn, so it must be your final trump card.

00:03:38.030 --> 00:03:42.110
And you used that trump card.  Am I correct?

00:03:42.520 --> 00:03:43.940
He knows.

00:03:44.150 --> 00:03:49.140
Even I was a bit worried because 
you greatly shrunk my lead.

00:03:49.240 --> 00:03:54.050
Yusei Fudo, I admire your 
card-playing instincts.

00:03:54.220 --> 00:03:56.410
But this is a team battle.

00:03:56.410 --> 00:04:00.190
The merits of individual players 
don't determine victory.

00:04:00.190 --> 00:04:06.140
I gave Andore and Breo a perfect strategy, 
so you only have three cards left in your deck.

00:04:06.140 --> 00:04:12.640
Even if I have barely any life points left, 
you'll lose the moment you can't draw a card.

00:04:14.110 --> 00:04:16.840
I set one card and end my turn.

00:04:17.560 --> 00:04:22.600
I'll make you run out of life 
points before I run out of turns!

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:24.200
My turn!

00:04:25.070 --> 00:04:28.080
Stardust, attack Rhinotaurus!

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:29.720
Shooting Sonic!

00:04:31.650 --> 00:04:33.450
It succeeded again!

00:04:33.700 --> 00:04:37.990
Yusei Fudo finally has more 
life points than Jean!

00:04:37.990 --> 00:04:43.100
Jean's life points are below the Riding 
Duel's safety line of 800 points!

00:04:43.100 --> 00:04:45.230
Yusei has 4 Speed Counters.

00:04:45.230 --> 00:04:48.600
If he activates Speed World 2's effect...

00:04:48.920 --> 00:04:51.920
I activate the Continuous 
Trap Thousand Crisscross!

00:04:52.160 --> 00:04:57.260
When my life points change, my life 
points become 1000 up to three times.

00:04:58.510 --> 00:05:01.990
Jean had a strategy to 
counteract Speed World 2!

00:05:01.970 --> 00:05:09.180
Yusei can't win unless he deals at least 
1000 points of damage in a single blow!

00:05:09.380 --> 00:05:11.650
In that case, Cosmic Blast!

00:05:12.010 --> 00:05:19.060
When a Dragon-Type Synchro Monster leaves the 
field, he takes damage equal to its attack points.

00:05:19.410 --> 00:05:24.700
On the next turn, he'll use Lightning 
Tricorn to destroy Stardust.

00:05:24.700 --> 00:05:26.750
I'll use that against him!

00:05:27.090 --> 00:05:29.870
I set one card and end my turn.

00:05:31.540 --> 00:05:32.710
My turn!

00:05:33.520 --> 00:05:35.820
I activate the trap Superficial Peace!

00:05:36.010 --> 00:05:36.650
What?

00:05:36.950 --> 00:05:41.830
On this turn, neither player 
can activate a spell or

00:05:41.830 --> 00:05:44.530
trap card, and monsters cannot 
be destroyed in battle.

00:05:44.530 --> 00:05:48.950
Lightning Tricorn attacks Stardust 
Dragon!  Gigavolt Charge!

00:05:53.440 --> 00:05:58.230
Due to Superficial Peace's 
effect, when you take damage...

00:05:58.470 --> 00:06:03.490
...one of your spell or trap cards 
is destroyed, and I draw one card.

00:06:06.070 --> 00:06:07.910
Cosmic Blast.

00:06:07.910 --> 00:06:11.440
If I carelessly attacked and 
destroyed Stardust Dragon...

00:06:11.440 --> 00:06:17.500
I would've taken damage equal to Stardust 
Dragon's attack points and lost.

00:06:18.290 --> 00:06:20.520
You were so close.

00:06:21.590 --> 00:06:24.200
I set two cards and end my turn.

00:06:25.580 --> 00:06:27.250
That was dangerous.

00:06:27.250 --> 00:06:30.660
If that trap succeeded, we would've lost.

00:06:30.810 --> 00:06:34.400
But Jean anticipated and countered it.

00:06:34.400 --> 00:06:39.670
Yeah.  Jean will never lose in 
a battle between strategists.

00:06:43.840 --> 00:06:45.770
He's strong.

00:06:45.910 --> 00:06:48.160
He sees through all my plans.

00:06:48.160 --> 00:06:49.440
Against someone like him...

00:06:50.740 --> 00:06:53.460
How can I win with only two cards in my deck?

00:06:54.310 --> 00:06:56.190
How can I beat him?

00:06:58.190 --> 00:06:59.110
Yusei...

00:06:59.300 --> 00:07:01.350
What's wrong with him?

00:07:01.350 --> 00:07:02.550
It can't be helped.

00:07:02.780 --> 00:07:05.470
He anticipated Yusei's every move.

00:07:05.470 --> 00:07:08.410
How can he beat him?

00:07:09.260 --> 00:07:10.560
Don't panic!

00:07:11.110 --> 00:07:12.080
Jack.

00:07:11.110 --> 00:07:12.080
Master Atlas.

00:07:12.080 --> 00:07:12.960
Be careful.

00:07:13.670 --> 00:07:14.850
Jack?

00:07:14.850 --> 00:07:16.670
But you're hurt!

00:07:17.110 --> 00:07:21.590
Yusei, how long are you planning 
to show me such pathetic dueling?

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:23.060
Jack!

00:07:29.170 --> 00:07:30.350
You too!

00:07:30.860 --> 00:07:34.320
As long as there's the slightest 
chance, never give up!

00:07:34.470 --> 00:07:39.050
The only thing you have 
to do is believe in Yusei!

00:07:40.720 --> 00:07:42.500
Yeah!  You're right!

00:07:43.120 --> 00:07:45.290
Yusei!  Do your best!

00:07:45.290 --> 00:07:47.030
Don't lose, Yusei!

00:07:47.030 --> 00:07:48.120
Yusei!

00:07:48.120 --> 00:07:49.670
All right!  Go, Yusei!

00:07:50.440 --> 00:07:51.350
Everyone...

00:07:52.420 --> 00:07:55.650
That's right.  This isn't just my battle.

00:08:00.260 --> 00:08:02.340
It's everyone's battle.

00:08:03.250 --> 00:08:06.180
I'll also believe in the 
possibility of winning!

00:08:06.930 --> 00:08:08.190
My turn!

00:08:09.890 --> 00:08:11.510
Good, it's here!

00:08:11.730 --> 00:08:14.180
I summon Synchron Explorer!

00:08:16.480 --> 00:08:20.520
When this card is summoned, 
I can Special Summon

00:08:20.520 --> 00:08:24.830
a Synchron from my graveyard 
by negating its effect!

00:08:25.390 --> 00:08:27.960
I Special Summon Junk 
Synchron from my graveyard!

00:08:31.080 --> 00:08:36.170
Level 3 Junk Synchron tunes 
Level 2 Synchron Explorer!

00:08:39.960 --> 00:08:43.620
The stars come together 
to call forth a new power!

00:08:43.620 --> 00:08:45.240
Become the path that lights the way!

00:08:45.800 --> 00:08:46.790
Synchro Summon!

00:08:47.410 --> 00:08:49.390
Come forth, Junk Warrior!

00:08:56.730 --> 00:08:58.740
Two Synchro Monsters?

00:08:59.460 --> 00:09:02.400
Beyond Synchro Summoning is Accel Synchro.

00:09:03.060 --> 00:09:07.330
After that day, I've been searching 
for new dueling possibilities.

00:09:11.580 --> 00:09:15.870
You Synchro Summoned a Synchro 
Monster during my turn?

00:09:16.180 --> 00:09:19.590
I haven't solved the Accel 
Synchro mystery yet.

00:09:19.820 --> 00:09:23.290
But this is the conclusion I've reached!

00:09:24.030 --> 00:09:26.580
I activate Speed Spell - Speed Fusion!

00:09:26.840 --> 00:09:28.550
Speed Fusion?

00:09:28.680 --> 00:09:35.610
I send the required cards on my field to the 
graveyard to Special Summon a Fusion Monster!

00:09:36.120 --> 00:09:40.780
Stardust Dragon and Junk Warrior, 
your powers become one!

00:09:41.780 --> 00:09:46.440
Fusion Summon!  Appear, 
Dragon Knight Draco-Equiste!

00:09:49.230 --> 00:09:50.640
Fusion Summon?

00:09:50.630 --> 00:09:52.130
Dragon Knight...

00:09:52.130 --> 00:09:53.220
...Draco-Equiste?

00:09:53.450 --> 00:09:55.240
What's this?

00:09:55.240 --> 00:10:00.150
Yusei Fudo's trump card wasn't 
just a Synchro Summon!

00:10:00.150 --> 00:10:01.250
What?

00:10:01.510 --> 00:10:04.980
Draco-Equiste attacks Lightning Tricorn!

00:10:05.400 --> 00:10:07.270
Spiral Javelin!

00:10:09.870 --> 00:10:12.440
I activate my trap Return Damage!

00:10:12.440 --> 00:10:17.790
This card stops me from taking battle 
damage, and you take that damage instead!

00:10:18.120 --> 00:10:22.030
I activate Dragon Knight Draco-Equiste's 
effect!  Wave Force!

00:10:22.300 --> 00:10:30.300
When your card effect deals damage to me, that 
effect is negated, and you take that damage instead!

00:10:32.650 --> 00:10:34.300
It worked!

00:10:34.300 --> 00:10:39.680
Yusei Fudo used his Fusion 
Monster to deal damage to Jean!

00:10:40.410 --> 00:10:42.210
You're incredible, Yusei!

00:10:42.210 --> 00:10:45.400
He summoned an incredible 
monster at the last moment!

00:10:46.340 --> 00:10:49.170
This is Yusei's growth.

00:11:08.140 --> 00:11:09.630
Fusion Summon...

00:11:10.460 --> 00:11:13.120
I can no longer read him?

00:11:14.330 --> 00:11:15.570
What's this?

00:11:16.150 --> 00:11:20.890
According to the data, he's 
never Fusion Summoned before.

00:11:26.700 --> 00:11:29.170
Even though he only has two turns left, it's

00:11:29.170 --> 00:11:33.030
too dangerous to wait for 
him to run out of cards.

00:11:33.610 --> 00:11:37.010
I activate Lightning Tricorn's effect!

00:11:37.010 --> 00:11:40.430
When this card is destroyed 
this turn, I can Special

00:11:40.430 --> 00:11:44.480
Summon either Thunder Unicorn or 
Voltic Bicorn from my Extra Deck!

00:11:44.480 --> 00:11:46.870
Come, Voltic Bicorn!

00:11:49.570 --> 00:11:53.170
Voltic Bicorn's effect is...

00:11:53.790 --> 00:11:56.890
When it's destroyed, I lose 
seven cards from my deck.

00:12:00.910 --> 00:12:03.270
He's planning to use my technique.

00:12:03.420 --> 00:12:09.570
This is bad!  If Voltic Bicorn attacks and 
self-destructs against Draco-Equiste...

00:12:09.570 --> 00:12:13.190
The final card in Yusei's deck 
will be sent to the graveyard!

00:12:13.190 --> 00:12:16.980
That means Yusei can't draw next turn.

00:12:16.980 --> 00:12:19.440
No way!  He's going to lose?

00:12:20.830 --> 00:12:22.920
I won't let you do that!

00:12:23.040 --> 00:12:25.630
I set one card and end my turn!

00:12:25.760 --> 00:12:28.370
That's pointless!  My turn!

00:12:29.340 --> 00:12:32.560
Voltic Bicorn attacks Draco-Equiste!

00:12:34.310 --> 00:12:35.780
Yusei!

00:12:36.170 --> 00:12:38.740
I activate the trap Scrap-Iron Scarecrow!

00:12:39.910 --> 00:12:40.490
What?

00:12:40.590 --> 00:12:44.100
This card negates your monster's attack.

00:12:44.100 --> 00:12:47.020
After it activates, I can 
set it on the field again.

00:12:47.400 --> 00:12:50.880
Whoa!  He used Scrap-Iron Scarecrow!

00:12:50.880 --> 00:12:53.750
He avoided running out of cards this turn!

00:12:54.680 --> 00:12:58.720
But your next turn will be your last turn!

00:12:58.720 --> 00:13:01.200
I set one card and end my turn!

00:13:01.680 --> 00:13:04.220
There's only one card left 
in Yusei Fudo's deck!

00:13:04.220 --> 00:13:07.220
Will he open the doors of 
victory on his final draw?

00:13:07.220 --> 00:13:10.090
Or will the door lead to defeat?

00:13:10.090 --> 00:13:11.880
This is the draw of destiny!

00:13:12.010 --> 00:13:13.060
Yusei...

00:13:13.600 --> 00:13:14.780
Please!

00:13:17.160 --> 00:13:20.750
Our entire team led to this card.

00:13:21.360 --> 00:13:23.050
It's our hope!

00:13:25.690 --> 00:13:26.620
My turn!

00:13:30.550 --> 00:13:32.770
I activate Speed World 2's effect!

00:13:33.110 --> 00:13:35.300
When I have 4 or more Speed Counters...

00:13:35.300 --> 00:13:41.500
I can remove 4 Speed Counters to deal 800 
points of damage for every Speed Spell in my hand!

00:13:45.100 --> 00:13:49.070
But due to Thousand Crisscross's 
effect, my life points return to 1000!

00:13:50.940 --> 00:13:55.150
That was the third time, so Thousand 
Crisscross's effect is gone!

00:13:55.320 --> 00:13:57.610
He no longer has his protective shield.

00:13:57.950 --> 00:13:59.860
It will all depend on the next strike!

00:13:59.860 --> 00:14:02.810
I activate Speed Spell - Overspeed!

00:14:03.180 --> 00:14:05.240
When I have 4 or more Speed Counters...

00:14:05.240 --> 00:14:08.100
I remove them all to add 
a Level 3-or-below monster

00:14:08.100 --> 00:14:12.560
and a spell or trap card 
in my graveyard to my hand!

00:14:13.100 --> 00:14:17.000
But I don't gain Speed 
Counters for three turns.

00:14:18.890 --> 00:14:22.690
I add Rapid Warrior and 
Reflect Barrier to my hand.

00:14:23.300 --> 00:14:24.610
I summon Rapid Warrior!

00:14:26.010 --> 00:14:29.640
Rapid Warrior can attack you directly!

00:14:29.640 --> 00:14:30.520
Nice!

00:14:30.520 --> 00:14:33.330
If this succeeds, Yusei will 
get a come-from-behind victory!

00:14:33.520 --> 00:14:36.460
Rapid Warrior, attack him directly!

00:14:39.300 --> 00:14:41.650
The Counter Trap Barrier Wave!

00:14:42.010 --> 00:14:44.420
I release one Synchro Monster on my field to

00:14:44.420 --> 00:14:48.640
switch all monsters on your 
field to defense position!

00:14:48.820 --> 00:14:52.590
Then you take damage equal to the 
attacking monster's defense points!

00:14:52.710 --> 00:14:53.460
What?

00:14:53.750 --> 00:14:55.910
I release Voltic Bicorn!

00:15:01.280 --> 00:15:06.440
Since Draco-Equiste is in defense 
position, it can't activate Wave Force.

00:15:06.430 --> 00:15:09.500
Take damage equal to Rapid 
Warrior's defense points!

00:15:13.490 --> 00:15:14.360
Yusei...

00:15:14.360 --> 00:15:16.080
Is there nothing he can do?

00:15:16.080 --> 00:15:21.620
Jean's strategy once again 
stopped Yusei Fudo's final blow!

00:15:23.130 --> 00:15:27.650
I remove the monster A/D Changer 
in my graveyard from play.

00:15:27.850 --> 00:15:31.250
Its effect switches Draco-Equiste 
to attack position!

00:15:33.490 --> 00:15:35.910
I set two cards and end my turn!

00:15:36.060 --> 00:15:38.550
Team 5D's turn is over!

00:15:38.780 --> 00:15:44.730
If Jean survives his next turn, 
Yusei's deck becomes zero and loses!

00:15:44.930 --> 00:15:49.800
Yusei Fudo, aren't you 
going to entertain me more?

00:15:49.940 --> 00:15:52.340
Show me your dueling!

00:15:52.760 --> 00:15:53.810
My turn!

00:15:54.900 --> 00:15:57.740
I activate the Continuous Trap Summon Tax!

00:15:58.070 --> 00:15:59.700
Is he finally executing his plan?

00:15:59.970 --> 00:16:03.800
If a player summons or Special 
Summons a monster this

00:16:03.800 --> 00:16:06.650
turn, he takes damage equal 
to half its attack points!

00:16:07.520 --> 00:16:13.260
He must have set Reflect Barrier, the card 
he added to his hand on the previous turn.

00:16:13.260 --> 00:16:14.340
In that case...

00:16:14.940 --> 00:16:23.980
If he summons a monster, he'll use Reflect 
Barrier to reflect Summon Tax's effect damage to me.

00:16:25.050 --> 00:16:31.060
But Summon Tax's effect damage 
equals half its attack points.

00:16:31.470 --> 00:16:37.320
To eliminate my 1000 life points, he has to 
summon a monster with at least 2000 attack points.

00:16:37.840 --> 00:16:39.380
Stop making me worry.

00:16:39.380 --> 00:16:43.990
The probability of summoning a monster 
that powerful is close to zero.

00:16:44.350 --> 00:16:47.300
I activate Speed Spell - Tyrant Force!

00:16:47.760 --> 00:16:52.900
Every time a card on your field is destroyed 
this turn, you take 300 points of damage!

00:16:53.170 --> 00:16:55.850
Then I activate Speed World 2's effect!

00:16:56.110 --> 00:17:01.230
By removing 10 Speed Counters, 
I destroy one card on the field!

00:17:01.530 --> 00:17:03.380
I'll break your combo!

00:17:03.380 --> 00:17:05.000
I destroy Summon Tax!

00:17:05.320 --> 00:17:06.930
I was waiting for that!

00:17:06.930 --> 00:17:07.430
What?

00:17:07.710 --> 00:17:11.400
I activate Dragon Knight 
Draco-Equiste's effect!

00:17:12.010 --> 00:17:16.110
By removing a Fusion-Material 
Synchro Monster from play...

00:17:16.110 --> 00:17:18.700
...Draco-Equiste gains that monster's 
effects until the End Phase!

00:17:19.400 --> 00:17:21.380
I remove Stardust Dragon 
in my graveyard from play!

00:17:21.730 --> 00:17:25.640
Draco-Equiste gains 
Stardust Dragon's effects.

00:17:25.640 --> 00:17:30.390
In other words, I can release this card to 
negate and destroy your card-destroying effect!

00:17:30.620 --> 00:17:31.370
What?

00:17:31.680 --> 00:17:33.490
I release Draco-Equiste!

00:17:33.490 --> 00:17:35.850
Go!  Victim Sanctuary!

00:17:39.050 --> 00:17:43.100
Draco-Equiste is Special Summoned 
from the graveyard at the End Phase!

00:17:43.250 --> 00:17:45.480
Draco-Equiste returns!

00:17:45.480 --> 00:17:47.320
This is what Yusei was aiming for!

00:17:47.320 --> 00:17:51.510
If the Summon Tax and Reflect 
Barrier combo succeeds...

00:17:51.510 --> 00:17:52.920
Yusei wins!

00:17:53.870 --> 00:17:56.320
My turn isn't over yet!

00:17:56.320 --> 00:17:59.050
I summon Hypnocorn!

00:17:59.390 --> 00:18:02.050
Due to Summon Tax's effect, 
you take damage equal to

00:18:02.050 --> 00:18:05.490
half of Hypnocorn's attack 
points, which is 700 points!

00:18:07.100 --> 00:18:14.930
But when Hypnocorn is summoned, I can 
destroy one set spell or trap card on the field!

00:18:14.930 --> 00:18:16.870
I destroy Reflect Barrier!

00:18:18.590 --> 00:18:20.510
That means the combo won't work!

00:18:20.510 --> 00:18:24.990
Due to Tyrant Force's effect, 
you take 300 points of damage!

00:18:27.160 --> 00:18:30.020
I flip over the trap card Chain Whirlwind!

00:18:30.250 --> 00:18:35.220
When a card effect destroys a card, 
two spell or trap cards are destroyed!

00:18:35.380 --> 00:18:38.420
I destroy Summon Tax and 
Scrap-Iron Scarecrow!

00:18:38.730 --> 00:18:40.730
The traps that Yusei set...

00:18:40.730 --> 00:18:42.400
...are all destroyed!

00:18:42.400 --> 00:18:46.610
Take Tyrant Force's effect again, Yusei!

00:18:48.700 --> 00:18:53.530
Yusei and Jean both have 300 
life points!  They're tied!

00:18:53.530 --> 00:18:57.830
And if Jean's turn ends, Team Unicorn wins!

00:18:57.830 --> 00:19:00.170
Oh no...  Yusei is going to lose...

00:19:00.170 --> 00:19:00.820
No way...

00:19:06.280 --> 00:19:09.130
I see the look in his eyes.

00:19:09.610 --> 00:19:12.450
He still thinks that he can make a comeback?

00:19:13.360 --> 00:19:17.330
Whoa, what's going on?  
He's not ending his turn?

00:19:17.790 --> 00:19:22.110
If I end my turn, my victory 
is mostly guaranteed.

00:19:22.490 --> 00:19:23.280
However...

00:19:24.880 --> 00:19:25.720
I...

00:19:28.070 --> 00:19:29.140
I...

00:19:33.830 --> 00:19:35.200
No way!

00:19:35.620 --> 00:19:39.300
Is Jean planning to attack?

00:19:39.300 --> 00:19:40.880
Maybe he is.

00:19:40.880 --> 00:19:44.420
Are you serious?  If he focuses 
on depleting his deck, we win!

00:19:45.020 --> 00:19:47.150
I know how Jean feels.

00:19:48.360 --> 00:19:50.580
Want to battle together?

00:19:50.810 --> 00:19:51.860
Together?

00:19:52.060 --> 00:19:57.570
Yeah.  If we form a team and battle, 
you're no longer battling solo.

00:19:57.570 --> 00:20:01.600
You must duel in a winning 
manner for the team.

00:20:01.820 --> 00:20:03.910
Duel in a winning manner...

00:20:04.950 --> 00:20:07.610
That's right.  Duel in a winning manner.

00:20:07.760 --> 00:20:12.550
Jean wants to defeat Yusei Fudo 
from the bottom of his heart.

00:20:13.920 --> 00:20:15.700
From the bottom of his heart...

00:20:17.690 --> 00:20:23.660
He's been waiting to meet an 
opponent that would change him.

00:20:25.960 --> 00:20:30.940
Yusei Fudo, I've never been 
this excited in a duel.

00:20:30.940 --> 00:20:34.850
All I want to do right now is defeat you!

00:20:35.740 --> 00:20:37.540
But I...

00:20:37.990 --> 00:20:42.750
Since he finally met a guy 
like him, he has to go for it!

00:20:45.030 --> 00:20:46.110
Go, Jean!

00:20:46.110 --> 00:20:49.880
Forget about the team and annihilate him!

00:20:51.440 --> 00:20:55.690
Yusei, here I go!  This 
will be my final strike!

00:20:55.690 --> 00:20:57.290
Bring it!  I'm looking forward to it!

00:20:57.810 --> 00:21:01.640
Whoa!  The duel continues!

00:21:01.640 --> 00:21:04.100
Don't lose!  Don't give up!

00:21:04.730 --> 00:21:07.570
Go, Hypnocorn!

00:21:07.850 --> 00:21:10.050
Attack Rapid Warrior!

00:21:10.050 --> 00:21:11.090
Go!

00:21:11.220 --> 00:21:12.480
Yusei!

00:21:13.940 --> 00:21:19.350
Everyone led me to this final card!

00:21:20.770 --> 00:21:24.460
I activate Stronghold Guardian's 
effect from my hand!

00:21:25.150 --> 00:21:26.790
What's that card?

00:21:27.080 --> 00:21:32.910
By sending Stronghold Guardian to the 
graveyard, Rapid Warrior gains 1500 defense points!

00:22:08.040 --> 00:22:12.710
The small cliff floats on the Milky Way

00:22:12.710 --> 00:22:17.720
The sights I see are different 
than what I imagined

00:22:17.980 --> 00:22:22.620
Were you able to move on from the past?

00:22:22.620 --> 00:22:27.630
The answer isn't no, but 
there's something missing

00:22:27.830 --> 00:22:32.500
The cruel god tests us

00:22:32.800 --> 00:22:39.440
Let's fill the emptiness 
and head to the next stage

00:22:39.440 --> 00:22:43.270
If you ask me "What's our relationship?"

00:22:43.270 --> 00:22:49.150
We're more than friends... 
but that's not quite right

00:22:49.310 --> 00:22:53.050
Bond is the proper word

00:22:53.050 --> 00:22:59.020
As we fight, we understand each other

00:22:59.020 --> 00:23:01.960
"Where are you right now?"  "On Earth"

00:23:01.960 --> 00:23:04.200
Because I'm not an astronaut

00:23:04.200 --> 00:23:08.870
I have no problems when 
I'm below the ozone layer

00:23:09.170 --> 00:23:11.740
"I know, I'm coming right away."

00:23:11.740 --> 00:23:15.210
You want to party until the morning

00:23:15.210 --> 00:23:18.440
At our special place
